# Files Claude Code should not read into context.
#
# Graphify writes its graph into the workspace on every extract. Left visible,
# each write invalidates the prompt cache and forces a full re-upload at
# cache-write rates on the next turn — and graph.json alone is 1.5 MB, so the
# cost is real. Graphify's own troubleshooting notes recommend exactly this.
#
# Nothing is lost by ignoring them: the graph is meant to be reached through
# `graphify query`, `graphify path` and `graphify explain`, which read the file
# from disk rather than needing it in context.
graphify-out/
graph.json
